    "Primary preparation interval starts after Runtime initialization and ends when all four segment functions are ready. Release/flush and whole-child/checker intervals are separate.",
    "Batch instrumentation establishes overlapping invocation lifetimes, not concurrent backend compilation or GPU execution.",
    "RUSAGE_CHILDREN high-water includes the fresh checker preparation helpers and is measured in Darwin bytes. Do not subtract before/after high-water or add RSS to Metal accounting. Batch RSS was higher in all three measured pairs.",
    "System/thermal/cache state were not controlled or sampled. These three pairs provide descriptive latency/memory observations, not a general performance guarantee."
